1555, "Secrets Revealed"

1556, "GTI Headquarters

We have located the GTI's base of operations- the Jotunheim installation in the Beta Aquilae system.

The full extent of their activities in Beta Aquilae remain unknown.  However, we believe the GTI has been studying Shivan culture and technology at Jotunheim since the massacre at Ross 128."

1557, "GTI Plans

Reconnaissance also has evidence of a large-scale prototype construction involving Shivan technology, but no data regarding the configuration and capability of this vessel could be gathered."

1558, "GTI Technology

GTI forces have access to Shivan armaments as well as the systems created by its research and development branch, so be advised your foe will possess superior technology.  You will have to fly smarter and fight harder to win this battle.

Command suspects the GTI may also have Shivan captives at Jotunheim for the purposes of biological research and the development of viral weapons."

1559, "Hades

Terran Command intercepted a GTI transmission and technical readout relating to a Jotunheim operation with the codename Project Hades.  Cryptographers are in the process of deciphering the transmission, and engineers are analyzing the technical readout.  Although we have nothing conclusive, we must act now."

1560, "Our Mission

The rogue Galactic Terran Intelligence group must be crushed.  These traitors threaten the security of the GTA, the stability of the Terran-Vasudan Alliance, and our future victory over the Shivans.  Report for your mission briefing, pilot."

1561, "Reconnaissance has uncovered the location of GTI's primary base of operations, the Jotunheim.  Details concerning the strength of the garrison remain sketchy.  GTA will launch an immediate, all-out offensive and deploy reinforcements as soon as possible."

1562, "Failure is not an option.  The GTI conducts weapons research on the Jotunheim, so be prepared to engage exotic prototypes with unknown capabilities."

1563, "Your cowardice jeopardized our best opportunity to eliminate the GTI threat.  Once operational, the Shivan-Terran hybrid will be invincible.  Dismissed, pilot."

1564, "Protect your bombers and keep your wingmen focused."

1565, "Excellent work!  Our initiative caught the GTI off guard.  Preliminary scans indicate the GTI possessed Shivan defensive technologies.  If that juggernaut had gone on line, GTI would be writing the history books."

1566, "For conspicuous gallantry at the risk of your own life, you have distinguished yourself above and beyond the call of duty in the highest traditions of military service.  You are hereby awarded the Galactic Service Medal, the most prestigious honor bestowed by the Galactic Terran Alliance."

1567, "That sucked, didn't it?  Well, if you share our feelings that Silent Threat had potential that it never managed to live up to, then you might like to try Silent Threat: Reborn.  ST:R is the Port team's reimagined and reinterpreted version of Silent Threat, with improved missions, a deeper plot, more immersion, and plenty of ties to FreeSpace 2!  Visit the Port website hosted at Hard Light Productions for more information."

1568, "Destroy Jotunheim"

1569, "Destroy Unknown"

1570, "Destroy the GTI Installation"

1571, "Destroy Unknown Vessel"

1572, "Capture GTI Installation"

1573, "All escape pods have been destroyed."

1574, "GTI vessels, power down and surrender."

1575, "Negative.  You have no authority in this system.  If you do not break off your attack, we will open fire."

1576, "Destroy GTI base Jotenheim."

1577, "Got something on my scanners!  Configuration unknown!  We're talkin' massive!"

1578, "GTA pilots, engage and destroy unknown vessel."

1579, "The vessel is reading as Terran but giving off Shivan electronics signatures.  Deploying reinforcements now."

1580, "The Jotunheim has jettisoned escape pods.  Destination: unknown vessel.  Intercept and destroy the pods."

1581, "Unknown vessel has been destroyed.  Well done, pilots.  Return to base."

1582, "Clash"

1583, "Terrans and Vasudans cruiser groups meet in a stand off.  Multiplayer mission.  Max respawns 10.  Recommended respawns 5."

1584, "Terran Command has initiated Operation Fury, a renewed offensive against Shivan positions in the Capella system.  Phase 1: eliminate all hostiles and secure the Vega system.  Reconnaissance has located a Hammer of Light cruiser group, comprised of two Aten-class warships, en route to the Beta Aquilae jump node.  Our task force has been deployed to engage and destroy this threat.  The Fenris-class Mjollnir and the Leviathan-class Dionysos will provide support for the assault."

1585, "Sensors indicate a Terran cruiser group on intercept course.  Engage and destroy the Mjollnir and Dionysos warships."

1586, "Our task force secured the Vega system, and Command has issued the go-ahead for Phase 2 of Operation Fury.  Excellent work, pilot."

1587, "You destroyed only one Aten warship.  Command has suspended Operation Fury until a more proficient force can secure the Vega system.  Anything less than total victory is unacceptable."

1588, "Guard your bombers and keep your wingmen focused."

1589, "Because of your failure, Command has scrapped Operation Fury.  With officers like you, the alliance needs no enemies."

1590, "Hammer of Light destroyed the Mjollnir and the Dionysos.  You are grounded pending a full investigation.  Dismissed, pilot."

1591, "Excellent work, pilot.  You destroyed the Mjollnir and the Dionysos."

1592, "A Terran warship survived the battle.  You failed to destroy both cruisers."

1593, "The Mjollnir and the Dionysos survived the battle.  You failed to destroy the Terran cruisers."

1594, "Both Aten cruisers survived the Terran attack.  In the divine scrolls it is written: ''In the blood of my enemy, my hands are sanctified.''"

1595, "Destroy enemy cruisers"

1596, "Protect Terran Cruisers"

1597, "Destroy Terran Cruisers"

1598, "Protect Vasudan Cruisers"

1599, "No Escape"

1600, "Intercept secret GTI science station before it gets away.  Capital ship stand off.  Multiplayer mission.  Max respawns 10.  Recommended respawns 5."

1601, "GTA reconnaissance has located the Ragnarok, a GTI science vessel.  Researchers on board the Ragnarok are developing the Serkr warhead, a megabomb of tremendous destructive power.  GTI scientists are now in the process of developing a warhead-viable containment system for the Serkr's volatile core."

1602, "Your objective is to destroy the Ragnarok and its Orion-class escort, the Heimdall.  For the sake of the Terran-Vasudan alliance, the Serkr project must be terminated."

1603, "Outstanding, pilot!  You destroyed the Ragnarok and the Heimdall.  Your efforts have terminated the GTI's Serkr project."

1604, "You destroyed the Ragnarok and terminated the GTI's Serkr project.  Command regrets you failed to eliminate the Heimdall, but you achieved your primary objective."

1605, "You are a disgrace, pilot.  The Ragnarok and the Heimdall escaped.  If GTI succeeds in stabilizing the Serkr warhead, every capital ship in the Terran-Vasudan alliance will be at risk.  Dismissed."

1606, "Use the explosive power of the Ragnarok to your advantage.  Let it get close to the Heimdall before destroying it."

1607, "Destroy Heimdall"

1608, "Destroy Ragnarok"

1609, "Destroy the Orion class destroyer"

1610, "Destroy Idun"

1611, "A GTI Leviathan-class cruiser has come through the jump node."

1612, "Pull back!  The Ragnarok's gonna blow!"

1613, "Stand Off"

1614, "Capital ship stand off.  Multiplayer mission.  Max respawns 10.  Recommended respawns 5."

1615, "Terran intelligence has received the coordinates of the Apophis, a Hammer of Light Typhon-class destroyer.  Your mission: ambush and obliterate this vessel."

1616, "The commander of the Apophis is Admiral Kek, the highest-ranking officer to defect since the formation of the Terran-Vasudan alliance and the HOL insurgency."

1617, "Deep-cover Vasudan operatives within Hammer of Light have advised intelligence of the destroyer's location.  Because we are the alliance force in closest proximity to these coordinates, command has ordered the GTD Hephaestus to launch an immediate attack."

1618, "The Epona has also been deployed to assist and will reinforce our assault once the cruiser is in position."

1619, "Expect to encounter heavy resistance.  Admiral Kek inspires absolute loyalty in his followers.  We must be willing to make any sacrifice necessary to destroy the Apophis."

1620, "Excellent work, pilot.  You destroyed the Apophis, and the GTD Hephaestus sustained only minor damage.  Command anticipates the death of Admiral Kek will undermine the morale and strategic leadership of Hammer of Light."

1621, "You eliminated Admiral Kek and his capital ship.  However, the GTD Hephaestus sustained heavy damage.  Extensive repairs will be required before we bring the ship back on line.  This may compromise allied operations in this sector."

1622, "Use some wingmen to defend the Hephaestus."

1623, "Command deeply regrets the loss of the GTD Hephaestus and its crew.  However, our task force accomplished its objective.  With the death of Admiral Kek and the destruction of the Apophis, the alliance has achieved a significant victory over Hammer of Light."

1624, "Command has ordered court-martial proceedings, pilot.  What should have been a triumph for the alliance resulted in humiliating defeat.  Admiral Kek and the Apophis destroyed the GTD Hephaestus and escaped."

1625, "Destroy Typhon"

1626, "Protect Orion"

1627, "HOL cruiser jumping in.  Protect the Hephaestus."

1628, "The Epona has jumped in."

1629, "Cry For Help"

1630, "You are sent in to protect a Vasudan destroyer under attack by Shivans.  Multiplayer mission.  Max respawns 10.  Recommended respawns 5."

1631, "The PVD Serket, a Typhon-class warship, has transmitted a distress call to allied forces in the Deneb system.  Two Lilith-class Shivan cruisers have engaged the Serket.  The Vasudan ship has sustained minor damage, but the Shivans have them outgunned.  Our mission: destroy the hostiles and save the Vasudan cruiser."

1632, "You saved the PVD Serket and obliterated the Shivans.  The Serket was able to complete its operations in the Deneb system, and the Vasudan admiralty has extended its gratitude.  Well done, pilot."

1633, "You neutralized the Shivan cruiser group, but the PVD Serket was destroyed.  Command has sent its regrets to the Vasudan admiralty.  Dismissed, pilot."

1634, "Use some wingmen to defend the Serket."

1635, "You are an embarrassment to the Terran fleet, pilot.  The Shivan destroyer vaporized the PVD Serket and escaped.  This failure may damage our alliance with the Vasudans, and you are grounded until further notice.  Dismissed."

1636, "Rescue Vasudan Destroyer"

